<title>USA: Harmon acquires Canadian affiliate.</title>
<headline>Harmon acquires Canadian affiliate.</headline>
<dateline>BLUE SPRINGS, Mo. 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harmon Industries Inc said Thursday it acquired its Canadian affiliate, Vale-Harmon Enterprises Ltd by purchasing 62 percent of Vale-Harmon's common stock.</p>
<p>Harmon said it now holds 100 percent of Vale-Harmon.</p>
<p>Harmon said it acquired the affiliate to offer a broader range of services to the Canadian rail market and allow its sales and engineering departments to deal directly with the customers. Vale-Harmon will continue to operate from its existing facilities.</p>
<p>Vale-Harmon is a sales and services supplier for Harmon and other manufacturers.</p>
<p>Harmon supplies signal and train control products.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
